Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 18:36:04 2026 +0000

    Carried lanterns: horn glows at the flame, a flame core, a lit hand
    
    Dino's beach shots (10 Nov 2026) showed the lit lantern's pane as a flat amber
    card, and in first person the fist holding it grey-dark.
    
    - The horn shell's flat material becomes HORN_GLOW_SHADER: brightest and
      most opaque at the flame's height, dimmer and clearer toward its top and
      bottom corners. The shader is made once and shared.
    - A small bright flame core (an 8x4 sphere) shows through the horn: a narrow
      candle tongue in the wooden lantern, a wider oil flame in the iron one
      (light_m over 10 m).
    - A short HandLight (0.6 m, 0.5 energy) just above the bail, as the torch
      has, so the fist is lit by the flame; too short to reach the ground.
    
    Only while lit; the dark twins are unchanged.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CZx7jASx6pGZ8KWpdsaQti

